e6505aaf29b2553d6415896e472b32422d1cd11f892b03ebdbebd0e1bbbc1c5" "q-72733/selection/f2eed07b05dde90fc4e3965630c8470296ca8fe86aa2c28fb24c677cb0839bc1" "q-72733/selection/00746981e07b21a36ca812581f862cd42c40ac42a1251a7c885115834467a4d0" "q-72733/selection/b4a685bfb525f630dcc57c0c589515cce036372d0bc0c5d796ac2a2bd0de239b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72733" :question/id #uuid "68e213ba-56c3-52ad-a2ef-a544dacede35" :question/math-academy-id "q-72733" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x=y+1 \\\\ x-y=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=1 \\\\ x-y=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72733/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72733"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102808/selection/6f158d79cdab796cc3dabbd7fc360ed1d5b254774c9f6e77dfd068483e09aea5" :answer/id #uuid "4d7ebea2-6028-56f1-94f6-58c564514eb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102808/selection/aeb31cc3ce58200b83376ba2919592026300dd995f8e0a3ece29b41e95b81db4" :answer/id #uuid "9ebd9aa1-0838-5623-8e6e-5cb815f79024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102808/selection/65025e1738b1f5be98a85218e5165ec191f5fccfa66b9285bb5cf0e635c075c8" :answer/id #uuid "6a00b159-494d-57f0-b2df-848c702a6c33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102808/selection/e3f7bebbd1d1b218174b40aafee77601623ac38ca0833ab8f11305232e25ac97" :answer/id #uuid "a24530fd-1240-5b73-957a-7bf1c97a3970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102808/selection/086da05b717a6a655496495fb54a020da05a4cbd1439011555a7c539c26989df" :answer/id #uuid "6dec4d8a-eb47-5a0e-8bc6-79e5c68ce845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102808/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86ed1587-7f70-5901-935f-5fea3708eadb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102808/selection/65025e1738b1f5be98a85218e5165ec191f5fccfa66b9285bb5cf0e635c075c8" :answer-field/choices ["q-102808/selection/6f158d79cdab796cc3dabbd7fc360ed1d5b254774c9f6e77dfd068483e09aea5" "q-102808/selection/aeb31cc3ce58200b83376ba2919592026300dd995f8e0a3ece29b41e95b81db4" "q-102808/selection/65025e1738b1f5be98a85218e5165ec191f5fccfa66b9285bb5cf0e635c075c8" "q-102808/selection/e3f7bebbd1d1b218174b40aafee77601623ac38ca0833ab8f11305232e25ac97" "q-102808/selection/086da05b717a6a655496495fb54a020da05a4cbd1439011555a7c539c26989df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102808" :question/id #uuid "380e10d6-e728-562d-9721-3838f62a9783" :question/math-academy-id "q-102808" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3=y \\\\ 3y=4x+2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=3 \\\\ -4x+3y=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102808/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102808"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806/field-1/acc1ee172ece246ca6aaed261576c2595cedee31387711f14fcefbe5a8e0fb90" :answer/id #uuid "a23924dd-cf30-52fc-b067-7a9dfc58b515" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806/field-1/d91744a5c266e927d72b0454bc3703b6092c60de074cab02ff1bf68f81fca69b" :answer/id #uuid "c4ba87ec-e1f4-5208-b832-c64fecbe5e45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "74985b79-99bb-584c-a522-f97c90ab03e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320806/field-1/acc1ee172ece246ca6aaed261576c2595cedee31387711f14fcefbe5a8e0fb90" :answer-field/choices ["q-320806/field-1/acc1ee172ece246ca6aaed261576c2595cedee31387711f14fcefbe5a8e0fb90" "q-320806/field-1/d91744a5c266e927d72b0454bc3703b6092c60de074cab02ff1bf68f81fca69b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "97ed901b-a6f8-551d-8594-b080ef99a2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d720bc03-f3d7-59a9-8d45-046322368859" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320806/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-320806/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806/field-3/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "c09e83c1-ca66-59b3-97a6-8b5d7c78ab0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f65ecc1-00c7-5a6c-8464-bd186c299b63" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320806/field-3/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-320806/field-3/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320806" :question/id #uuid "7174a34a-7912-56f7-9a7a-e80574460128" :question/math-academy-id "q-320806" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y=5 \\\\ 4x+y=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $11$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $11$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320806/field-1" "q-320806/field-2" "q-320806/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320806"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320847/field-1/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer/id #uuid "b69ac83f-0fe7-5de6-ae09-774ffc93be92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320847/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "93962f49-2332-57a5-bff3-ea2b3cb5b169" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320847/field-1/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer-field/choices ["q-320847/field-1/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320847/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1aea10e8-7b2e-597f-8caa-9898a705b2d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320847/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "adb5d11e-fe50-551b-85f2-cf7ca9e59ae2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320847/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-320847/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320847/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a3738ad2-254c-51f2-bac1-4a926f1ea273" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320847/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "acb9124e-56c0-5068-a34f-6032aab2ca3c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320847/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-320847/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320847" :question/id #uuid "6783007e-1f5e-5332-be6d-e39947617e57" :question/math-academy-id "q-320847" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 4x=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $6$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 4x+y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-320847/field-1" "q-320847/field-2" "q-320847/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321441/field-1/fe408bb8584d9549e0a0c9ef3adf534b4545b6ad8bd71384d7efac8421910872" :answer